SUMMARY:IJGLS Symposium
DESCRIPTION:Climate change\, pollution\, and biodiversity loss are intens
 ifying worldwide\, and their heaviest burdens fall on the world's most vu
 lnerable populations and indigenous communities. An estimated 1.5 billion
  people lack basic access to redress for environmental harms through poli
 tical\, administrative\, or legal channels. Many of these communities als
 o lack skilled advocates\, and the lawyers and nonlawyers who do take up 
 their causes face growing harassment and physical attacks.  The Indiana J
 ournal of Global Legal Studies has brought together scholars from across 
 the Americas to examine where marginalized communities\, their advocates\
 , and the governance systems that too often leave them behind intersect.F
 or a full list of panels and presenters\, view the full schedule here (ht
 tps://events.iu.edu/live/files/8597-ijgls-symposium-fall-2026-schedulepdf
 ).&#160\;  Papers presented at the symposium will be published in Volume 
 34 Issue 2 of the Journal.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Climate change\, pollution\, and biodiv
 ersity loss are intensifying worldwide\, and their heaviest burdens fall 
 on the world's most vulnerable populations and indigenous communities. An
  estimated 1.5 billion people lack basic access to redress for environmen
 tal harms through political\, administrative\, or legal channels. Many of
  these communities also lack skilled advocates\, and the lawyers and nonl
 awyers who do take up their causes face growing harassment and physical a
 ttacks.</p><p>  The <em>Indiana Journal of Global Legal Studies</em> has 
 brought together scholars from across the Americas to examine where margi
 nalized communities\, their advocates\, and the governance systems that t
 oo often leave them behind intersect.</p><p><strong>For a full list of pa
 nels and presenters\, <a class="file file_8597 lw_files_pdf" title="ijgls
 -symposium-fall-2026-schedule.pdf" href="https://events.iu.edu/live/files
 /8597-ijgls-symposium-fall-2026-schedulepdf" target="_blank" rel="noopene
 r">view the full schedule here</a>.&#160\;</strong></p><p>  Papers presen
 ted at the symposium will be published in Volume 34 Issue 2 of the Journa
 l.</p>
UID:20261120T144500Z-2464840@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261027T100702Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2464840-ijgls-symposium
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112T203324Z
